# REDNET Georgia collector — environment configuration. Copy to .env in the
# collector's own deployment directory on REDNET (NEVER commit a real .env).
# See docs/georgia-remote-collector.md for the full setup walkthrough.

# Base URL of production's reverse-proxied internal collector API (TLS
# terminates at the proxy, NOT in this process — see the deployment doc for
# why and how). Must include the scheme, e.g. https://collector.example.com
GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_PRODUCTION_BASE_URL=https://REPLACE_ME

# Must be IDENTICAL to production's GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_HMAC_SECRET (see
# production's own .env) — generate with, e.g.:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# and copy the SAME value to both machines. Never commit this value.
GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_HMAC_SECRET=REPLACE_ME

# Local-only SQLite file for this collector's own operational state (feed
# frontier/seen-protocol tracking + the retry outbox) — NOT a copy of
# production's database, never synced anywhere.
GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_DB_PATH=/home/collector/georgia-collector/state/collector.db

# Optional overrides — defaults shown match production's current schedule
# (see settings.fine_monitor.public_feed_times/timezone). Keep these in
# sync with production manually if production's schedule ever changes.
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_RUN_TIMES=09:00,15:00,21:00,23:55
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_TIMEZONE=Asia/Tbilisi
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_SOURCE_URL=https://police.ge/protocol/index.php?lang=en
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=30
# police.ge requests and the short production endpoints (plates/bootstrap-
# pending/health) use GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_REQUEST_TIMEOUT above. Submitting a
# feed-match/bootstrap-result can legitimately take minutes server-side when
# several genuinely-new fines each need synchronous translation before the
# response returns — this separate, longer timeout avoids a false client-
# side timeout/retry on that specific path (the outbox already makes a
# genuine timeout safe either way, this just reduces noise).
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_SUBMISSION_TIMEOUT=180
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Inbound check-now server (see "Fix the Georgia public bot Check Now
# flow") — the opposite direction from everything above: production calls
# INTO this process for a single live plate lookup (🔎 Проверить сейчас
# can't wait for the next scheduled collector cycle). Bind host should be
# this machine's WireGuard address (e.g. 10.50.0.2), NOT 0.0.0.0 — never
# directly internet-facing, same principle as production's own
# collector_api_host. Port is deliberately different from
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_PRODUCTION_BASE_URL's port (8765) since these are two
# independent directions of the same HMAC-authenticated exchange.
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_CHECKNOW_HOST=127.0.0.1
# GEORGIA_COLLECTOR_CHECKNOW_PORT=8766
